   "html": "<h2>ZeroStick EXO Terms of Use, Device Licence and Limited Warranty</h2>\n<blockquote><p><strong>DRAFT FOR LAWYER REVIEW.</strong> This draft is not in force yet. Words in [CAPITALS IN BRACKETS] are filled in after the review (WIRING.md, section 6).</p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>Version:</strong> 2026-10-10-draft</p>\n<p>These terms cover:</p>\n<ul><li>the <strong>ZeroStick EXO app</strong> on PC, phone and tablet;</li><li>the <strong>firmware</strong> that runs inside the ZeroStick EXO device;</li><li>the EXO's <strong>limited warranty</strong>.</li></ul>\n<p>They are the app's terms of use and the device's licence (sometimes called an &quot;EULA&quot;) in one document, so there is one thing to read.</p>\n<h3>The most important points</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>One purchase, no subscription.</strong> You buy the EXO once. The app and every firmware update are free with it. There is no subscription for the app or the device, ever. (EXO Studio, our separate optional PC app, has its own terms.)</li><li><strong>Game rules and bans.</strong> Using an adapter like the EXO, and its aim assist, Smart Actions, scripts and vision features, can break a game's or a platform's rules. <strong>A game can ban your account for it, and a console can block devices like the EXO.</strong> Using it online is your choice and your risk. Section 7.</li><li><strong>Your data stays with you.</strong> See the Privacy Policy.</li><li><strong>Returns and warranty</strong>: 30-day returns through our store, plus the EXO's 1-year limited warranty against defects in section 11.</li><li><strong>Disputes.</strong> We try to settle problems with you first. If that fails, disputes are decided by individual arbitration, not in court, and <strong>not as class actions, with no jury</strong>. Small claims court is always open to either of us. You can <strong>opt out within 30 days</strong> by email. Section 15.</li></ul>\n<h3>1. Who these terms are between</h3>\n<p>These terms are an agreement between you and Reliable Trend Enterprises LLC, a California limited liability company doing business as ZeroStick, at 7426 Cherry Ave, Ste 210 #1062, Fontana, CA 92336, United States (&quot;ZeroStick&quot;, &quot;we&quot;, &quot;us&quot;).</p>\n<p>You agree to them by tapping or clicking &quot;I agree&quot; in the app, or by using the app or the EXO.</p>\n<p><strong>Where we sell.</strong> The EXO is sold in the United States. We do not sell it in the EU, the EEA or the UK yet.</p>\n<p><strong>Age.</strong> You must be at least 13 to use the app. If you are under 18, or under the age of majority where you live, a parent or guardian must agree to these terms for you.</p>\n<p><strong>Buying.</strong> Buying the EXO is covered by our store's terms and policies on zerostickgaming.com. Where the store's terms and these differ about the purchase itself, the store's terms apply. These terms cover using the app and the device.</p>\n<h3>2. Your licence</h3>\n<p><strong>The app.</strong> The app is free. We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use it to set up and use ZeroStick devices you own or are allowed to use.</p>\n<p><strong>Personal use only.</strong> You may use the app and the EXO for your own personal, non-commercial use, and only in lawful ways. Streaming or recording yourself playing is fine. Using them to run a paid service for others (for example selling &quot;boosting&quot;, or playing on other people's accounts) is not.</p>\n<p><strong>The firmware.</strong> The firmware is the software inside the EXO. It is licensed, not sold, to whoever owns the EXO at the time, for use on that EXO only. If you sell or give away your EXO, the licence goes with it, and these terms then apply to the new owner.</p>\n<p><strong>What you may not do:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>copy the firmware onto other hardware, or sell or share the app or the firmware separately from the EXO;</li><li>reverse engineer, decompile or take apart the app or the firmware, except where the law allows it whatever these terms say, or where an open-source licence allows it;</li><li>get around the EXO's update-signature check, or install firmware that is not ours;</li><li>remove our notices or other people's copyright notices;</li><li>use the app or the EXO to break the law or someone else's rights.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Open-source parts.</strong> The app and the firmware include open-source software. Each part is under its own licence, listed in Settings &gt; Legal &gt; Open-source licences (<a href=\"#\" data-legal-doc=\"notices\">THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md</a>). Nothing in these terms limits what those licences let you do.</p>\n<p><strong>We keep ownership</strong> of the app, the firmware, our game packs and our designs, apart from the open-source parts.</p>\n<h3>3. Updates</h3>\n<ul><li>We may offer updates to the app and the firmware. They are free.</li><li>Firmware updates are installed from the app, over your cable or Bluetooth, and only when you choose to.</li><li>The EXO checks that each update is signed by us, and refuses one that is not.</li><li>Keep the cable connected and the devices powered during an update.</li><li>Some features may need the latest firmware.</li></ul>\n<h3>4. Your configs, scripts and other content</h3>\n<p><strong>Yours stays yours.</strong> Configs, scripts, settings, pictures and other things you make belong to you (or whoever made them). They stay in your app and on your EXO. We get no rights to them unless you send them to us, for example for support. Then you let us use them only to help you.</p>\n<p><strong>Other people's content.</strong> You can bring in content made by others:</p>\n<ul><li>GPC scripts;</li><li>XIM share codes;</li><li>Smart Action codes;</li><li>vision packs from a link;</li><li>configs someone sends you.</li></ul>\n<p>Make sure you are allowed to use it. Other people's content can behave in ways you do not expect. We do not check, approve or support it, and we are not responsible for it.</p>\n<p><strong>Sharing.</strong> If you share a config or a code, you are responsible for what it contains and for having the right to share it.</p>\n<h3>5. Compatibility with other formats</h3>\n<p>The app can read some formats that other products use, such as GPC scripts and XIM share codes. We built this from public information. It does not mean that the makers of those products are connected with us (see <a href=\"#\" data-legal-doc=\"trademarks\">TRADEMARKS-AND-AFFILIATION.md</a>). We do not promise that every script or code works the same way.</p>\n<h3>6. Game packs and vision features</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Game packs and vision packs</strong> read what the game shows on screen to help with things such as weapon detection, aim and shot timing.</li><li><strong>Games change.</strong> A game update can stop a pack working until we update it. We do not promise that any pack works with any particular game or version.</li><li><strong>Vision features need a capture card</strong> and the right setup. The EXO works only from the video picture and your controller's signal. It does not read or change a game's memory or files.</li></ul>\n<h3>7. Game rules, bans and fair play</h3>\n<p><strong>Please read this section.</strong></p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Warning.</strong> Using a controller adapter like the EXO may break a game's or a platform's rules, and can get your game account restricted or banned. Consoles and games may also detect or block devices like it. Whether you use it online is your choice, and your risk.</p></blockquote>\n<ul><li><strong>Games have their own rules.</strong> Most online games have terms of service or a code of conduct. Many forbid aim assistance, automatic timing, macros, scripts, or devices that change or add to your controller input. Some publishers name devices like the EXO, or features the EXO offers, as not allowed, and use anti-cheat systems to look for them.</li><li><strong>Using the EXO can get your game account banned</strong>, for a while or for good, and can cost you items, progress or purchases in that game. We cannot prevent this, undo it, or make up for it.</li><li><strong>You are responsible</strong> for knowing and following the rules of each game, platform and event where you use the EXO, and for the choices you make. Where a game's rules do not allow a feature, do not use it there.</li><li><strong>We do not encourage anyone to break a game's rules.</strong> We do not promise or claim that the EXO is &quot;undetectable&quot;, and we do not help anyone avoid anti-cheat systems.</li><li><strong>What the EXO is, and is not.</strong> The EXO works at the level of the controller signal: it takes the input from your controller (or mouse and keyboard), can adjust it, and sends controller input to your console, much as a different controller or an assistive device would. With a capture card, its vision features look at the same video picture you see. It is not a hack of any game. It does not read, change or inject into a game's code, memory or files, and does not change your console's software.</li><li><strong>Games and consoles can block it.</strong> A console maker, platform or game publisher may detect, restrict or disable controller adapters, or features like the EXO's, at any time, including by an update. If that happens, or an account is banned or restricted, it is not a fault in the EXO, and we do not owe compensation for it. Your 30-day return (section 10), the limited warranty (section 11) and your rights under consumer law are not affected.</li><li><strong>Why the EXO exists.</strong> ZeroStick is an accessibility-first company, founded by a disabled gamer. The EXO exists to reduce the precision, speed and strength that console games demand, so more people can play: any controller, or a mouse and keyboard, on any console.<ul><li>Where a game or platform has its own accessibility settings or allows assistive devices, we encourage you to use those routes.</li><li>A game's rules still apply to you whatever your reason for using the EXO.</li></ul></li><li><strong>No competitions.</strong> Do not use aim assist, automatic timing or automation in any tournament, league or competition with prizes or rankings that does not explicitly allow it.</li></ul>\n<h3>8. Acceptable use</h3>\n<p>Do not use the app or the EXO to:</p>\n<ul><li>break any law or anyone's rights;</li><li>harass, cheat or defraud other people;</li><li>run a paid service for others, such as &quot;boosting&quot; or account services (section 2);</li><li>spread malware or harmful scripts;</li><li>interfere with other people's devices, accounts or networks.</li></ul>\n<h3>9. Using the device safely</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>The EXO sends real controller input to your console.</strong> Configs, scripts and Smart Actions can behave in ways you do not expect: a press that comes early or late, a stick that moves on its own, or input that keeps going.<ul><li>Learn how to stop it: unplug the EXO, or use your config's stop button if it has one.</li><li>Do not use it where unexpected input could hurt anyone or damage anything.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Look after it.</strong> Keep the EXO dry, away from heat, and out of reach of small children. Use the cables and power the manual describes.</li><li><strong>Do not open it.</strong> Opening the case, or changing the hardware or the firmware, can damage it and is not covered by the warranty.</li><li><strong>Accessibility aid, not a medical device.</strong> The EXO is an assistive gaming device. It is not a medical device, and it is not made for any safety-critical use.</li><li>[REGULATORY STATEMENTS, e.g. FCC PART 15 NOTICE AND ANY CALIFORNIA PROPOSITION 65 WARNING, IF REQUIRED; see WIRING.md.]</li></ul>\n<h3>10. Returns</h3>\n<p>You can return the EXO under our store's refund policy: <strong>30 days</strong>, as described at zerostickgaming.com/policies/refund-policy. We reply to return requests within 1 to 2 business days. Write to caleb@zerostickgaming.com or call (323) 680-4706, Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm Pacific Time.</p>\n<h3>11. Limited warranty</h3>\n<p><strong>What is covered.</strong> We warrant to the first buyer that the EXO will be free from defects in materials and workmanship, under normal use, for <strong>1 year</strong> from the date of delivery. (Controllers sold by ZeroStick carry their own <strong>5-year stick warranty</strong>, as our store's policies describe.)</p>\n<p><strong>What we will do.</strong> If a covered defect appears during the warranty, we will repair or replace the EXO, at our choice, or refund what you paid if we cannot do either. A repaired or replacement EXO is covered for the rest of the original warranty.</p>\n<p><strong>What is not covered:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>damage from accidents, misuse, liquid or the wrong power supply;</li><li>opening the EXO, or changing its hardware or firmware;</li><li>normal wear;</li><li>problems caused by other products, by game or console updates, or by a game's restrictions or bans;</li><li>a console maker, platform or game publisher blocking, detecting or disabling the EXO or its features, or banning or restricting an account. We do not give compensation for these (section 7). Refunds that consumer law or this warranty require still apply;</li><li>cosmetic damage that does not affect how it works.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Damage that is not a defect.</strong> If your EXO is damaged in a way the warranty does not cover (for example it was dropped, got wet or was misused), contact us anyway. If you send it back to us for repair, we may be able to offer a discount on the repair. This is at our discretion and decided case by case; it is not a promise of a free or discounted repair. The free shipping above is only for covered defects.</p>\n<p><strong>How to claim.</strong> Email caleb@zerostickgaming.com with your order number and what is wrong. We will tell you how to send it back.</p>\n<p><strong>Shipping.</strong> For a covered defect, we pay all the shipping, both ways: to us, and the repaired or replacement EXO back to you.</p>\n<p><strong>Your other rights.</strong> This warranty gives you specific legal rights, and you may have others that vary by state. To the extent the law allows, implied warranties (such as merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose) last only as long as this limited warranty. Some states do not allow limits on how long an implied warranty lasts, so that limit may not apply to you.</p>\n<h3>12. Disclaimers</h3>\n<p>Apart from the limited warranty in section 11, and to the extent the law allows, the app, the firmware and our game and vision packs are provided &quot;as is&quot;. We do not promise that:</p>\n<ul><li>they are free of errors;</li><li>they suit every need, setup or disability;</li><li>they work with every game, console, controller, capture card or version;</li><li>they will not be detected or restricted by any game.</li></ul>\n<h3>13. Limits on our liability</h3>\n<p>To the extent the law allows:</p>\n<ul><li>we are not liable for <strong>indirect or consequential losses</strong>, including losses from a game account being banned or restricted, or losing in-game items, progress or purchases;</li><li>our <strong>total liability</strong> for all claims about the app, the firmware and the EXO is limited to the greater of (a) <strong>what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim</strong> (for example, for the EXO), or (b) <strong>US$100</strong>.</li></ul>\n<p>These limits do not cover death or personal injury caused by our negligence, fraud, or anything else the law does not let us limit. Where the law does not allow a cap, the cap does not apply. Nothing here reduces your rights under section 11 or under consumer law.</p>\n<h3>14. Indemnity</h3>\n<p>To the extent the law allows, you agree to cover our reasonable losses and costs if someone else makes a claim against us because of your breach of these terms, your breach of a game's or platform's rules, or content you share.</p>\n<h3>15. Disputes and arbitration</h3>\n<p><strong>Please read this section. It affects how disputes are settled, and it includes a waiver of class actions and of a jury.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>15.1 Talk to us first.</strong> Most problems can be solved quickly. Before either of us starts arbitration or a court case, the one with the complaint sends the other a short written notice: your name, your order number, what the problem is and what you want. You send yours to caleb@zerostickgaming.com (or by post to the address in section 20); we send ours to the email address you gave us when you ordered or wrote to us. We then both try in good faith to settle it for <strong>60 days</strong> from the notice. Time limits for bringing the claim are paused during those 60 days.</p>\n<p><strong>15.2 Arbitration instead of court.</strong> If it is not settled, any dispute, claim or disagreement between you and us that arises from or relates to the app, the firmware, the EXO or these terms (including whether this section applies) is decided by <strong>binding individual arbitration</strong>, not in court, except as 15.3 says.</p>\n<ul><li>The arbitration is run by the <strong>American Arbitration Association (AAA)</strong> under its <strong>Consumer Arbitration Rules</strong>, and, where they apply, its rules for mass filings (15.6). The rules are at adr.org.</li><li>One neutral arbitrator decides. The hearing is held by video or phone, or on documents only if the claim is small, unless the arbitrator decides an in-person hearing is needed. An in-person hearing takes place in the county where you live, or another place we both agree.</li><li>The arbitrator can award you the same individual relief a court could, including damages, and must follow these terms and the law.</li><li><strong>Fees.</strong> Your share of the filing fee is no more than the AAA's consumer fee schedule allows a consumer to be charged. <strong>We pay all other AAA fees and the arbitrator's fees.</strong> Each side pays its own lawyer, unless the law or the arbitrator says otherwise.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15.3 What stays out of arbitration.</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Small claims court.</strong> Either of us may bring an individual claim in small claims court instead, if it qualifies, and keeps it there.</li><li><strong>Intellectual property.</strong> Either of us may ask a court to stop the misuse of copyrights, trademarks or other intellectual property.</li><li><strong>Public injunctive relief.</strong> A request for an order that protects the general public, where California law does not allow it to be waived, is decided by a court after any arbitration of the individual claims, and is paused until then.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15.4 Only individual claims; no jury.</strong> You and we each bring claims only for ourselves, <strong>not as a plaintiff or class member in any class, collective or representative action</strong>. The arbitrator may not combine more than one person's claims, or award relief to anyone other than the person bringing the claim. <strong>You and we give up the right to a jury trial</strong> for every claim that this section sends to arbitration.</p>\n<p><strong>15.5 You can opt out.</strong> You may opt out of this section within <strong>30 days</strong> of first agreeing to these terms, by emailing caleb@zerostickgaming.com with your name, your order number and the words &quot;I opt out of arbitration&quot;. Opting out does not affect anything else in these terms. Disputes are then decided in court under 15.8.</p>\n<p><strong>15.6 Many claims at once (&quot;mass arbitration&quot;).</strong> If 25 or more similar claims are brought against us, or by us, by the same or coordinated lawyers or organisations within 180 days, they are handled under the AAA's <strong>Mass Arbitration Supplementary Rules</strong>:</p>\n<ul><li>the claims go forward in batches;</li><li>a small first group is decided first, so that both sides can learn from the results and try to settle the rest;</li><li>the deadlines for the others are paused meanwhile.</li></ul>\n<p>Nothing in this paragraph takes away anyone's right to have their own claim decided, or makes a consumer pay more than 15.2 says.</p>\n<p><strong>15.7 If part of this section cannot be enforced.</strong> If the class-action waiver in 15.4 is found unenforceable for a claim, that claim (and only that claim) goes to court, not to arbitration. If any other part of this section is unenforceable, the rest still applies.</p>\n<p><strong>15.8 Courts.</strong> Any dispute that goes to court under this section (or because you opted out) is decided only by the state or federal courts in <strong>San Bernardino County, California</strong>, unless the law lets you bring your claim where you live. You and we agree to those courts' jurisdiction.</p>\n<p><strong>15.9 Changes to this section.</strong> If we change this section, the change does not apply to a dispute we already knew about. You may reject the change by emailing us within 30 days of it, and the earlier version of this section then applies to you.</p>\n<p><strong>15.10 Outside the US.</strong> This section does not apply to consumers who live outside the United States. If you live in the EU, the EEA or the UK (where we will sell later), you may bring a claim in the courts where you live, and EU consumers can also use their national consumer dispute services.</p>\n<h3>16. Governing law</h3>\n<p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, USA, and US federal law (including the Federal Arbitration Act for section 15), without regard to rules about conflicts of laws. If you live in the EU, the EEA, the UK or another country with consumer protections that cannot be set aside, you keep those protections.</p>\n<h3>17. Ending these terms</h3>\n<ul><li>You can stop using the app at any time.</li><li>We may suspend or end your licence if you seriously or repeatedly break these terms. Where it is fair and allowed, we warn you first.</li><li>Sections 4, 7 and 11 to 17 stay in force after these terms end.</li></ul>\n<h3>18. Changes to these terms</h3>\n<p>We may update these terms. The new version gets a new date, with a summary of what changed at the top. If a change matters, the app shows you the new version and asks you to agree before you carry on. A change does not apply to a dispute that started before it.</p>\n<h4>What changed in this version</h4>\n<ul><li>First version.</li></ul>\n<h3>19. General</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Whole agreement.</strong> These terms, the Privacy Policy and our store's policies for your purchase are the whole agreement about the app and the EXO.</li><li><strong>If one part is unenforceable</strong>, the rest still applies.</li><li><strong>If we do not enforce a term at once</strong>, we can still enforce it later.</li><li><strong>Transfers.</strong> We may transfer these terms to a company that takes over the EXO, and you keep the same rights. The firmware licence passes with the EXO (section 2).</li><li><strong>Events outside our control.</strong> We are not responsible for delays caused by things we cannot reasonably control.</li><li><strong>Export.</strong> Do not use or export the EXO where US or other applicable sanctions or export laws forbid it.</li></ul>\n<h3>20. Contact</h3>\n<p>Reliable Trend Enterprises LLC (ZeroStick), 7426 Cherry Ave, Ste 210 #1062, Fontana, CA 92336, United States. Email: caleb@zerostickgaming.com Phone: (323) 680-4706, Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm Pacific Time.</p>"
