   "html": "<h2>ZeroStick EXO App and Device Privacy Policy</h2>\n<blockquote><p><strong>DRAFT FOR LAWYER REVIEW.</strong> This draft is not in force yet. Words in [CAPITALS IN BRACKETS] are filled in after the review (WIRING.md, section 6).</p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>Version:</strong> 2026-10-10-draft<br><strong>Applies to:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>the ZeroStick EXO app, on Windows (the PC app) and later on iPhone, iPad and Android;</li><li>the ZeroStick EXO device and its firmware;</li><li>the ZeroStick Calibration Dongle screens inside the app.</li></ul>\n<p>EXO Studio, our separate paid PC app, has its own privacy policy.</p>\n<h3>The short version</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>We do not collect your data.</strong> The app has no account, no sign-in, no ads, no analytics and no crash reporting. Nothing you do in it is sent to us.</li><li><strong>Your configs live on your EXO and in the app on your phone or PC.</strong> They travel between the two over a USB cable or Bluetooth, not over the internet.</li><li><strong>Your game video stays between your capture card, your EXO and your app.</strong> The EXO reads it to run vision features and keeps it only in memory. It is never sent to us.</li><li>The app goes online only when you ask it to, for example to fetch a vision pack from a link you paste (section 5).</li><li>We do not sell or share personal information.</li></ul>\n<h3>1. Who we are</h3>\n<p>The app and the EXO are made by Reliable Trend Enterprises LLC, a California limited liability company doing business as ZeroStick, at 7426 Cherry Ave, Ste 210 #1062, Fontana, CA 92336, United States (&quot;ZeroStick&quot;, &quot;we&quot;, &quot;us&quot;).</p>\n<p>Contact: caleb@zerostickgaming.com, or (323) 680-4706 (Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm Pacific Time).</p>\n<p><strong>Where we sell.</strong> The EXO is sold in the United States. We do not sell it in the EU, the EEA or the UK yet. The parts of this policy about those places are ready for when we do; we will then name our EU and UK representatives here.</p>\n<p><strong>Our online store</strong> (zerostickgaming.com, on Shopify) has its own privacy policy. It covers what you give us when you buy, such as your name, address and payment.</p>\n<h3>2. What stays in the app, on your phone or PC</h3>\n<p>The app keeps these on the phone or PC it runs on. We cannot see them.</p>\n<div class=\"lg-tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Your configs and every setting in them: button mappings, aim and stick settings, Smart Actions, macros, GPC scripts you add, and the name and colour you give each one</td><td>so you can edit them and send them to your EXO</td></tr><tr><td>App settings: theme, text size, high contrast, reduce motion, which product you last used, when your EXO was last seen</td><td>your preferences</td></tr><tr><td>Pictures you choose for a config (made smaller)</td><td>shown on the config's card. Stored only in the app, and never sent to the EXO or to us</td></tr><tr><td>A config, a code or a curve you copy</td><td>kept on the clipboard, which you control</td></tr><tr><td>For the Calibration Dongle screens: the Bluetooth name and ID of your dongle, your script names, an interrupted firmware update, your language choice, your calibration history, and the last controller you calibrated (its model, colour and serial number)</td><td>to reconnect, resume and show your history</td></tr><tr><td>On the PC: the app window's size and position, in a temporary file</td><td>to open the window the way you left it</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Removing it:</strong> Settings &gt; Factory reset clears the EXO screens' saved settings and configs on that phone or PC. Uninstalling the app removes everything above. Factory reset also clears the pictures you chose for your configs. It does not clear the Calibration Dongle screens' data: those screens are kept separate from the EXO screens and keep their own, until you uninstall the app. Your configs on the EXO itself stay there until you delete them or reset the EXO.</p>\n<p><strong>Phone backups.</strong> On Android, the app turns off Android's app backup, so its data is not copied into your phone's backup to your Google account. On iPhone and iPad, an iCloud or computer backup of your device may include the app's data; your device's settings control this.</p>\n<h3>3. What stays on your EXO</h3>\n<div class=\"lg-tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Your configs (the same settings as above, including GPC scripts and the values they save)</td><td>so the EXO works without the app</td></tr><tr><td>Calibration, and small settings such as which mode the EXO is in</td><td>so it remembers how it is set up</td></tr><tr><td>A device ID: a code worked out from the EXO's own network hardware address</td><td>so the app can tell your EXOs apart. It stays between the EXO and your app</td></tr><tr><td>Bluetooth pairing keys, on EXO models with Bluetooth</td><td>so your phone reconnects without pairing again</td></tr><tr><td>Wi-Fi network name and password, on EXO models with Wi-Fi, only if you set them</td><td>to join your network</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Resetting the EXO to factory settings erases your configs and settings on it.</p>\n<p><strong>What the EXO handles but does not keep:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Your controller's buttons and sticks, and your keyboard and mouse.</strong> The EXO reads them and sends them on to your console. This happens live, and nothing is saved.</li><li><strong>Your capture card's video.</strong> The EXO decodes the picture to run vision features, such as reading the weapon name or a shot meter. Frames are held in memory only. If you open a vision screen in the app, the app may ask the EXO for a single picture so you can set things up. That picture goes over your cable or Bluetooth to your app, and nowhere else.</li><li><strong>Headset audio and your headset microphone</strong>, with consoles and controllers that use this feature. Sound is passed live between your console and the headset plugged into your controller. It is never recorded or stored.</li></ul>\n<h3>4. How the app and the EXO talk</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>USB cable</strong>: the PC app talks to the EXO over its USB-C cable.</li><li><strong>Bluetooth Low Energy</strong>, on EXO models and phones that use it: the phone app talks to the EXO over Bluetooth. The connection stays between your phone and your EXO.</li><li><strong>Wi-Fi</strong>, on EXO models with Wi-Fi, only if you turn it on: the EXO joins your home network for features that need it. The EXO does not connect to our servers or to any other internet service.</li><li><strong>The Calibration Dongle screens</strong> talk to the dongle over USB (WebHID), Bluetooth, or the dongle's own Wi-Fi hotspot.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Firmware updates</strong> come from the app over the same cable or Bluetooth link. The EXO checks that each update is signed by us and refuses one that is not. The EXO never downloads anything from the internet by itself.</p>\n<h3>5. When the app goes online</h3>\n<p>The app has no account, analytics, advertising, crash reporting or automatic update check. It goes online only in these cases:</p>\n<ol><li><strong>A vision pack link you paste</strong> (PC app). The PC app fetches the pack's description, and then the pack, from the web address you gave it. Like any download, that website sees your PC's internet address. The app only accepts secure (https) public addresses, and only reads the pack. It never runs anything from it.</li><li><strong>Links you open</strong>, such as our store or a help page. They open in your own browser.</li></ol>\n<p>Game packs, game data, firmware files and XIM share-code decoding are all inside the app. Using them sends nothing anywhere.</p>\n<h3>6. Permissions the phone app asks for</h3>\n<div class=\"lg-tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Permission</th><th>Why</th><th>Is anything sent to us?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bluetooth</td><td>to find and connect to your EXO and your Calibration Dongle</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Location (Android, iPhone)</td><td>Android and iOS require it for an app to find Wi-Fi networks and some Bluetooth devices. The app uses it only to connect to the Calibration Dongle's Wi-Fi hotspot. It never reads your location</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Local network (iPhone)</td><td>to talk to the Calibration Dongle on its hotspot</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Photos, or a file picker</td><td>only when you choose a picture for a config</td><td>No. It stays in the app</td></tr><tr><td>Microphone</td><td>only in the Calibration Dongle's controller test, to check that a controller's built-in microphone works. The sound is measured live and never recorded</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Internet</td><td>for a vision-pack link you paste, and the links you open</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>7. Planned features</h3>\n<p>We may later add an <strong>optional, off-by-default</strong> count of how many people use the app. If we do, we will:</p>\n<ul><li>update this policy first;</li><li>ask you before anything is sent;</li><li>give you a switch to turn it off.</li></ul>\n<p>Until then, nothing like it exists in the app or the EXO.</p>\n<h3>8. Sharing and selling</h3>\n<ul><li>We do not sell your personal information.</li><li>We do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising (California's terms).</li><li>We do not receive it from the app or the EXO in the first place.</li></ul>\n<p>If you email or call us for support, we use what you tell us only to help you. We keep it for [SUPPORT RETENTION, e.g. 2 YEARS] after your last message. If you send us a config or a log, we use it only to fix your problem.</p>\n<h3>9. Your rights</h3>\n<p>Because the app and the EXO send us nothing, the data is in your hands. You can see it, change it and delete it in the app, and on the EXO.</p>\n<p>For anything we do hold (support messages, and what our store holds about your order), you can ask us to show it to you, correct it or delete it. Email caleb@zerostickgaming.com.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>California and other US states with privacy laws</strong>: you have the rights those laws give you, and we will not treat you differently for using them.</li><li><strong>EU, EEA and UK</strong>: when we sell there, you will have the GDPR rights, including the right to complain to your data protection authority.</li></ul>\n<p>We answer within 45 days.</p>\n<h3>10. Children</h3>\n<p>The app and the EXO are not meant for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, of any age, through the app or the EXO.</p>\n<h3>11. Security</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Firmware updates</strong> must be signed by us, and the EXO refuses any that are not.</li><li><strong>Vision pack links</strong> are limited to secure, public web addresses.</li><li><strong>On Bluetooth EXO models</strong>, pairing uses Bluetooth's secure connection.</li><li><strong>Configs on your EXO</strong> are stored without encryption. Anyone with the EXO in hand and the right tools could read them. Keep that in mind before putting anything private in a config's name.</li></ul>\n<h3>12. Changes to this policy</h3>\n<p>If we change this policy, the new version gets a new date, with a summary of what changed at the top. If a change matters, the app shows it to you before you carry on.</p>\n<h4>What changed in this version</h4>\n<ul><li>First version.</li></ul>\n<h3>13. Contact</h3>\n<p>Reliable Trend Enterprises LLC (ZeroStick), 7426 Cherry Ave, Ste 210 #1062, Fontana, CA 92336, United States. Email caleb@zerostickgaming.com. Phone (323) 680-4706, Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm Pacific Time.</p>"
