   "file": "ACCESSIBILITY-STATEMENT.md",
   "version": "2026-10-10-draft",
   "draft": true,
   "html": "<h2>ZeroStick EXO App Accessibility Statement</h2>\n<blockquote><p><strong>DRAFT FOR LAWYER REVIEW.</strong> Words in [CAPITALS IN BRACKETS] are filled in after the review.</p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>Version:</strong> 2026-10-10-draft. Last checked: 10 October 2026, by reading the app's code. No hands-on test with assistive technology has been done yet.</p>\n<h3>Our commitment</h3>\n<p>ZeroStick was started by a disabled gamer. The EXO exists so that more people can play console games: any controller, or a mouse and keyboard, on any console, with help for precision, speed and strength. The app you use to set it up should be just as easy to use.</p>\n<p><strong>Our target is WCAG 2.2 level AA</strong> for the app on PC, phone and tablet. We are not there everywhere yet. This page says what works, what does not, and how to tell us about a barrier.</p>\n<h3>What works today</h3>\n<p><strong>Ease of Access settings</strong> (Settings &gt; Ease of Access):</p>\n<ul><li>dark, light and &quot;match my device&quot; themes, plus a pure-black (OLED) theme;</li><li>larger text (Large, Extra large);</li><li>high contrast;</li><li>reduce motion, which also turns moving device pictures into still ones;</li><li>bigger touch targets;</li><li>&quot;Show help buttons&quot;: every &quot;?&quot; opens a plain explanation. Help is never removed, only hidden if you choose.</li></ul>\n<p>The app also follows your device's own &quot;reduce motion&quot; and &quot;increase contrast&quot; settings.</p>\n<p><strong>Screen readers:</strong> buttons, switches and controls carry names for screen readers (several hundred labelled controls). Changing status, such as &quot;connected&quot;, is announced. Keyboard focus is shown clearly.</p>\n<p><strong>Controller-first:</strong> most setup can be done with sensible defaults. Plain words are used throughout.</p>\n<p><strong>The device helps too:</strong> the EXO lets you use the controller that suits you, remap any button, play with a mouse and keyboard, and add help for aim and timing.</p>\n<h3>Known problems</h3>\n<ol><li><strong>Not yet tested with a screen reader by a person.</strong> The labels are in the code, but nobody has gone through the app with VoiceOver, TalkBack, NVDA or Narrator yet.</li><li><strong>Windows High Contrast (forced colours) is not specially handled</strong>, so some parts may look wrong with it on.</li><li><strong>The Calibration Dongle screens</strong> are based on a separate open-source tool, with a different design. They have not been checked to the same level as the rest of the app.</li><li><strong>Language.</strong> The main app is in English only. The Calibration Dongle screens are in 23 languages.</li><li><strong>Pictures and drawings</strong>, such as controller drawings, curves and live video from your capture card, have no full text version.</li><li><strong>Some game-pack pictures</strong> are publishers' artwork without a text description. The game's name is shown next to them in text.</li></ol>\n<h3>What we are doing next</h3>\n<ul><li>Test the main screens with VoiceOver, TalkBack and NVDA, with disabled players taking part ([TARGET DATE]).</li><li>Support Windows forced colours ([TARGET DATE]).</li><li>Bring the Calibration Dongle screens up to the same level ([TARGET DATE]).</li></ul>\n<h3>Tell us about a barrier</h3>\n<p>If something in the app or the EXO is hard or impossible for you to use, we want to know. You will not be asked to prove a disability.</p>\n<ul><li>Email: caleb@zerostickgaming.com</li><li>Phone: (323) 680-4706, Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm Pacific Time. If you use a relay service, call through it.</li></ul>\n<p>Tell us what you were trying to do, what got in the way, and what you use, if you are happy to. We reply within 1 to 2 business days, and tell you within [PLAN TIME, e.g. 10 BUSINESS DAYS] what we will do and by when.</p>\n<h3>Standards and laws</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Standard:</strong> WCAG 2.2 level AA, applied to the apps through W3C's WCAG2ICT guidance.</li><li>EXO Studio (our PC app) and our website have their own statements.</li><li>[LEGAL STATUS SENTENCE, after the lawyer's view on the ADA and, before EU sales, the European Accessibility Act.]</li></ul>\n<h4>What changed in this version</h4>\n<ul><li>First version.</li></ul>"
