r><td>Ed25519 signature check for updates</td><td>—</td><td>Derived from TweetNaCl, public domain</td></tr><tr><td>Weapon-name and weapon-picture recognition networks</td><td>ZeroStick</td><td>Our own networks. They were trained on game screenshots, which belong to the games' publishers</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>C. The radio chip firmware (ESP32-C6, on EXO models with Bluetooth or Wi-Fi)</h3>\n<div class=\"lg-tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Licence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Espressif esp_hosted 3.0.7 slave firmware, unmodified, with ESP-IDF and NimBLE</td><td>Apache-2.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>D. The console-facing chip firmware (RP2040)</h3>\n<div class=\"lg-tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Licence</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GP2040-CE (ZeroStick fork with a UART input)</td><td>MIT</td><td>Open Stick Community. ZeroStick's additions are MIT</td></tr><tr><td>Raspberry Pi Pico SDK 2.2.0</td><td>BSD-3-Clause</td><td>Raspberry Pi Ltd</td></tr><tr><td>TinyUSB</td><td>MIT</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Pico-PIO-USB (patched)</td><td>MIT</td><td>sekigon-gonnoc</td></tr><tr><td>Other libraries bundled by GP2040-CE (such as nanopb, ArduinoJson)</td><td>[CHECK each against the GP2040-CE tree at commit 5fb6404; see WIRING.md]</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>GP2040-CE's LGPL-licensed Xbox 360 security module (xsm3) is <strong>left out</strong> of our build on purpose, and the build fails if it is ever linked.</p>\n<h3>E. Licence texts and required notices</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>Apache-2.0</strong> (ESP-IDF and its components, AndroidX): licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, the software is distributed on an &quot;AS IS&quot; BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND.</li><li><strong>MIT and BSD parts</strong>: each part's copyright notice and licence text must go with the app and the firmware. Their full texts are in <a href=\"#\" data-legal-doc=\"licences\">LICENCE-TEXTS.md</a>, shown in the app in Settings &gt; Legal &gt; Licence texts. [ENGINEERING: the CC BY 4.0 and SIL OFL 1.1 texts, and Node.js's own LICENSE, are still to be added there; see WIRING.md.]</li><li><strong>CC BY 3.0 and CC BY 4.0</strong>: the credits above, and in the app's Credits.</li></ul>\n<h3>What changed in this version</h3>\n<ul><li>First version.</li></ul>"
