   "html": "<h2>Trademarks and affiliation</h2>\n<blockquote><p><strong>DRAFT FOR LAWYER REVIEW.</strong> Words in [CAPITALS IN BRACKETS] are filled in after the review.</p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>Version:</strong> 2026-10-10-draft</p>\n<h3>We are independent</h3>\n<p>The ZeroStick EXO, its app and its firmware are made by Reliable Trend Enterprises LLC, doing business as ZeroStick. <strong>We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by or approved by any of these companies</strong>, and they have not reviewed our products:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Game publishers and studios</strong>, including:<ul><li>Activision Publishing (Call of Duty);</li><li>Electronic Arts and Respawn Entertainment (Apex Legends, Battlefield);</li><li>Take-Two Interactive, 2K and Visual Concepts (NBA 2K);</li><li>the makers of any other game named in the app.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Console and platform makers</strong>: Sony Interactive Entertainment (PlayStation, DualSense, DualShock), Microsoft (Xbox, Windows), Nintendo (Nintendo Switch), Apple (iPhone, iPad) and Google (Android).</li><li><strong>Other controller-adapter, scripting and accessory makers</strong>: ConsoleTuner (Titan Two), Collective Minds (Cronus Zen), XIM Technologies (XIM), Razer, Logitech and others whose products the EXO works with.</li></ul>\n<h3>Why other companies' names appear</h3>\n<p>We use other companies' names only to say truthfully what the EXO works with. For example:</p>\n<ul><li>&quot;works with DualSense controllers&quot;;</li><li>&quot;a game pack for NBA 2K27&quot;;</li><li>&quot;reads GPC scripts&quot; and &quot;imports XIM share codes&quot;.</li></ul>\n<p>This is sometimes called &quot;nominative use&quot;. We do not use other companies' logos to suggest a connection, and nothing we say implies that they support or endorse the EXO.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Game packs and vision packs</strong> are made by ZeroStick, or by the person who shared them, from what the game shows on screen. They are not official products of any game.</li><li><strong>GPC and XIM compatibility</strong>: the app can read GPC scripts and XIM share codes. We built this from public information. The EXO is not a Cronus, Titan or XIM product, and those companies do not support it.</li></ul>\n<h3>Trademarks</h3>\n<ul><li>Activision and Call of Duty are trademarks of Activision Publishing, Inc.</li><li>Apex Legends and Battlefield are trademarks of Electronic Arts Inc.</li><li>NBA 2K is a trademark of Take-Two Interactive Software, Inc.</li><li>PlayStation, DualSense and DualShock are trademarks of Sony Interactive Entertainment Inc.</li><li>Xbox and Windows are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies.</li><li>Nintendo Switch is a trademark of Nintendo.</li><li>Apple, iPhone and iPad are trademarks of Apple Inc.</li><li>Android and Google Play are trademarks of Google LLC.</li><li>Titan Two is a trademark of ConsoleTuner.</li><li>Cronus and Cronus Zen are trademarks of Collective Minds Gaming Co. Ltd.</li><li>XIM is a trademark of XIM Technologies.</li><li>Bluetooth is a trademark of Bluetooth SIG, Inc.</li><li>[LAWYER: CHECK EACH OWNER'S EXACT LEGAL NAME AND WHETHER EACH MARK IS REGISTERED.]</li><li>Other names are the trademarks of their owners.</li></ul>\n<p>ZeroStick and EXO are trademarks of Reliable Trend Enterprises LLC. [REGISTRATION STATUS: e.g. ® ONLY ONCE REGISTERED; ™ UNTIL THEN.]</p>\n<h3>Game pictures</h3>\n<p>The game and weapon pictures in the app belong to the games' publishers. They are shown only to identify the game or weapon a pack works with. They are not licensed to us, and showing them does not mean the publisher made, approved or endorses the EXO. If you own one of these pictures and want it removed, write to us and we will take it out of the next update.</p>\n<h3>Controller button pictures</h3>\n<p>The controller buttons in the app are drawn from Kenney's free &quot;Input Prompts&quot; pictures (public domain, CC0) and by ZeroStick. The home button is a <strong>generic glyph we drew ourselves</strong>: a house for a PlayStation or Nintendo controller's home button, and a ring with a plain cross for an Xbox controller's guide button. They are not the PlayStation logo, the Xbox logo or any Nintendo mark, and they are used only to show which button to press.</p>\n<h3>Questions</h3>\n<p>If you represent one of these companies and have a concern, please write to caleb@zerostickgaming.com. We will answer promptly.</p>"
